INT. LIGHTHOUSE KITCHEN - MORNING

Salt-stained windows. Two mugs. A kettle starting to rattle.

ROSALIE (60s, cardigan) cracks eggs. Her sister CONSTANCE (60s, cardigan) slices bread. Same hands. Same sigh.

                    ROSALIE
          Connie, sit.

                    CONSTANCE
          Rosie, I'm fine.

She isn't. She grips the counter. Rosalie sets down the bowl.

                    ROSALIE
          Did you take the pills?

                    CONSTANCE
          Did you?

                    ROSALIE
          Yes.

                    CONSTANCE ^
          Yes.

They speak together. They stop. The kettle shrieks. Neither moves.

Constance turns the burner off. She pours. Her hands are steady now.

                    CONSTANCE (CONT'D)
          She said I could stay.

                    ROSALIE
          Who?

                    CONSTANCE
          The woman from the county. She told her I could stay.

Rosalie sits. Slowly.

                    ROSALIE
          Connie, there was no woman.

Constance smiles, sets a mug before her, and says nothing.
